@node In Lean Buffer
@section In Lean Buffer

@multitable {aaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Key
@tab Command
@tab Effect
@item @samp{C-c C-e}
@tab @code{eglot}
@tab Start Eglot@comma{} the LSP client
@item @samp{C-c C-r}
@tab @code{lena-eglot-restart-file}
@tab Reprocess the file@comma{} building out-of-date imports first
@item @samp{C-c C-i}
@tab @code{lena-infoview}
@tab Toggle the infoview (needs Lean 4.30 or later)
@item @samp{C-c C-c}
@tab @code{project-compile}
@tab Build the project; suggests @samp{lake build}
@item @samp{C-h .}
@tab @code{eldoc-doc-buffer}
@tab Show goals and expected type@comma{} when there's no infoview
@item @samp{C-\}
@tab @code{toggle-input-method}
@tab Turn the @code{Lena} input method off and on
@item @samp{C-u C-x =}
@tab @code{describe-char}
@tab Describe the character at point@comma{} and how to type it
@item @samp{M-g i}
@tab @code{imenu}
@tab Jump to a definition in the buffer
@end multitable

The @code{Lena} input method is on in Lean buffers@comma{} shown as @samp{∃∀} in the mode line:
For example@comma{} @samp{\a} gives @samp{α}@comma{} @samp{\to} gives @samp{→}@comma{} and @samp{\\} a backslash.

@node In the Infoview
@section In the Infoview

The infoview follows point and shows the goals@comma{} the expected type and Lean's
messages on the current line. While Lean builds the imports@comma{} it shows Lake's
output.

@multitable {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Key
@tab Command
@tab Effect
@item @samp{n} / @samp{p}
@tab @code{lena-infoview-next-goal}
@tab Next / previous goal
@item @samp{w}
@tab @code{lena-infoview-copy-goal}
@tab Copy the goal
@item @samp{v}
@tab @code{lena-infoview-view-options}
@tab Menu of what the infoview shows
@item @samp{i} @samp{t} @samp{a} @samp{l} @samp{r} @samp{d}
@tab 
@tab Toggle instances@comma{} types@comma{} inaccessible names@comma{} let values@comma{} target first@comma{} diffs
@item @samp{TAB}
@tab 
@tab Fold a heading@comma{} or expand a trace
@item @samp{RET}@comma{} @samp{mouse-1}
@tab 
@tab Press a button@comma{} like @samp{[apply]}@comma{} or go to a message's position
@end multitable

On a subterm of a goal:

@multitable {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Key
@tab Command
@tab Effect
@item @samp{RET}@comma{} @samp{mouse-1}@comma{} @samp{C-h .}
@tab @code{lena-infoview-describe}
@tab Describe it in @samp{*Lena Help*}: explicit form@comma{} type@comma{} docs
@item @samp{M-.} / @samp{M-@comma{}}
@tab @code{xref-find-definitions}
@tab Go to its definition / come back
@end multitable

Hovering a subterm shows its explicit form and type with ElDoc (in a popup with
@uref{https://github.com/casouri/eldoc-box, eldoc-box}) and@comma{} with @code{tooltip-mode}@comma{} in a tooltip; setting @code{use-system-tooltips}
to @samp{nil} formats these better. In @samp{*Lena Help*}@comma{} @samp{l} and @samp{r} go back and forth.

@node Signs in the Margin
@section Signs in the Margin

While Eglot manages the buffer@comma{} @code{lena-margin-mode} shows signs in the left
margin in place of Flymake's indicators. Hovering a sign shows its message;
clicking it lists all diagnostics.

@multitable {aaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Sign
@tab Meaning
@item @samp{‼} / @samp{!}
@tab Error / warning or note on this line
@item @samp{┌} @samp{│} @samp{└}
@tab A diagnostic spanning several lines
@item @samp{✓}
@tab Complete proof
@item @samp{✗}
@tab Unsolved goals; the proof goes on here
@item @samp{⚠}
@tab Declaration that uses @samp{sorry}
@item orange @samp{│}
@tab Lean is still processing these lines
@end multitable

@node With Evil
@section With Evil

With the @code{lena-evil} package@comma{} @samp{(with-eval-after-load 'evil (lena-evil-setup))}
binds these keys in the infoview's normal state:

@multitable {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Key
@tab Effect
@item @samp{]g} / @samp{[g}
@tab Next / previous goal
@item @samp{]h} / @samp{[h}
@tab Next / previous heading
@item @samp{gr}
@tab Refresh
@item @samp{K}
@tab Describe the subterm
@item @samp{<localleader> v}
@tab View options
@item @samp{<localleader> y}
@tab Copy the goal
@end multitable

In @samp{*Lena Help*}@comma{} @samp{C-o} and @samp{C-i} go back and forth. In Doom Emacs@comma{} @samp{K}@comma{} @samp{gd} and
@samp{C-o} describe@comma{} go to a definition@comma{} and come back.

