@node Manual
@subsection Manual

First clone the Git repository@comma{} then@comma{} in your Emacs initialization file@comma{} add
Lena to @code{load-path} and load it. For lazy loading the autoloads-file needs to be
built beforehand.

@lisp
;; git clone https://github.com/ISTA-PLV/lena.git ~/path/to/lena

(add-to-list 'load-path "~/path/to/lena/lena")
;; For Evil:
;; (add-to-list 'load-path "~/path/to/lena/lena-evil")

;; Option 1@comma{} eager loading:
(require 'lena)
;; (require 'lena-evil)

;; Option 2@comma{} lazy loading:
;; cd ~/path/to/lena && ./build.el autoloads
;; (require 'lena-autoloads)
;; (require 'lena-evil-autoloads)

;; Optionally@comma{} make the README available as an Info manual:
(require 'info)
(info-initialize)
(add-to-list 'Info-directory-list "~/path/to/lena/lena")
@end lisp

@node Installation via @code{package-vc}
@subsection Installation via @code{package-vc}

Emacs' @code{use-package} macro supports a @samp{:vc} keyword as interface to
@code{package-vc}. (Because each package has autoload-cookies on relevant
expressions@comma{} and because @code{use-package} will load the autoloads-file that is
generated at installation@comma{} you don't need to specify load-triggers like @samp{:mode}.
I.e. lazy-loading should work out of the box.)

@lisp
(use-package lena
  :vc ( :doc "lena/README.org"
        :lisp-dir "lena"
        :url "https://github.com/ISTA-PLV/lena.git"))

;; For Evil:
;; (use-package lena-evil
;;   :after (lena evil)
;;   :vc ( :lisp-dir "lena-evil"
;;         :url "https://github.com/ISTA-PLV/lena.git")
;;   :config (lena-evil-setup))
@end lisp

@node Install for Doom Emacs
@section Install for Doom Emacs

Doom's own @samp{:lang lean} module uses upstream Nael@comma{} so disable it: in
@samp{~/.doom.d/init.el}@comma{} comment out @samp{lean} under @samp{:lang}. Then declare Lena in
@samp{~/.doom.d/packages.el}:

@lisp
(package! lena
  :recipe (:host github :repo "ISTA-PLV/lena"
           :files ("lena/*.el" "lena/lena.info" "lena/lena.texi"
                   "lena/NOTICE" "lena/LICENSE*")))
;; With Evil:
(package! lena-evil
  :recipe (:host github :repo "ISTA-PLV/lena"
           :files ("lena-evil/*.el" "lena-evil/LICENSE")))
@end lisp

Set it up in @samp{~/.doom.d/config.el}@comma{} with its keys under the local leader @samp{SPC
m}@comma{} then run @samp{doom sync} and restart Emacs:

@lisp
;; Lean's Unicode input@comma{} such as \to for →@comma{} is on in Lean buffers; C-\
;; toggles it.  Start the Lean server:
(add-hook 'lena-mode-local-vars-hook #'eglot-ensure 'append)

(map! :after lena
      :map lena-mode-map
      :localleader
      :desc "Infoview"           "i" #'lena-infoview
      :desc "Restart file"       "r" #'lena-eglot-restart-file
      :desc "Build project"      "b" #'project-compile
      :desc "ElDoc buffer"       "e" #'eldoc-doc-buffer)

(map! :after lena-infoview-buffer
      :map lena-infoview-mode-map
      :localleader
      :desc "Refresh"            "r" #'lena-infoview-refresh
      :desc "View options"       "v" #'lena-infoview-view-options
      :desc "Copy goal"          "y" #'lena-infoview-copy-goal)

;; The infoview places itself@comma{} in a side window by default; see
;; `lena-infoview-display-action'.  The help buffer is a popup.
(set-popup-rule! "^\\*Lena Infoview\\*" :ignore t)
(set-popup-rule! "^\\*Lena Help\\*" :slot 2 :vslot -8 :size 0.42 :select t)

;; With Evil:
(after! (evil lena-infoview-buffer)
  (lena-evil-setup))
@end lisp

In the infoview's normal state@comma{} @samp{]g} and @samp{[g} go to the next and previous goal@comma{}
@samp{]h} and @samp{[h} to headings@comma{} @samp{gr} refreshes@comma{} and on a subterm @samp{K} or @samp{RET} describes it@comma{}
@samp{gd} goes to its definition and @samp{C-o} comes back. The descriptions open in
@samp{*Lena Help*}@comma{} where @samp{C-o} and @samp{C-i} go back and forth and @samp{q} closes.

@node Configuration
@section Configuration

Below@comma{} we highlight some of Lena's user options; for the complete list@comma{} use
@samp{M-x customize-group RET lena RET}.

You can bind custom keys in @code{lena-mode-map}:

@lisp
(keymap-set lena-mode-map "C-c ." #'highlight-symbol-at-point)
@end lisp

To automatically enable features (e.g. Eglot) when Lena is started@comma{} customize
@code{lena-mode-hook} as follows:

@lisp
(add-hook 'lena-mode-hook #'eglot-ensure)
@end lisp

