@node Flymake and Margin
@subsection Flymake and Margin

The signs in the margin can be changed@comma{} for example@comma{} with chickens below. Play
around with the value for @code{lena-margin-emoji-height} to scale your chosen
characters to the line height.

@lisp
(setq lena-margin-goals-accomplished "🐣"  ; complete proof
      lena-margin-unsolved-goals "🥚"      ; unsolved goals
      lena-margin-admitted "🍗"            ; uses sorry
      lena-margin-emoji-height 1)          ; as tall as text lines
@end lisp

To keep Flymake's indicators instead of the signs@comma{} set @code{lena-margin} to @samp{nil}@comma{}
before visiting a Lean file.

Lena truncates the trace of Flymake@comma{} only showing "(trace)"@comma{} as in VS Code.
To keep the full text in Flymake instead@comma{} set @code{lena-eglot-widgets} to @samp{nil}
before Lean starts.

To start Lean buffers with the input method off@comma{} set @code{lena-activate-quail} to
@samp{nil}; @samp{C-\} still turns it on. To keep your global default input method
instead@comma{} set @code{lena-prepare-quail} to @samp{nil}.

