@node Reporting Problems
@section Reporting Problems

When something looks wrong@comma{} @samp{M-x lena-snapshot} records the state of Lena@comma{} Eglot
and Lean under @code{lena-snapshot-directory}; call it before restarting anything. Its
most useful part is Eglot's events log@comma{} which Eglot limits to 2 MB and Doom
Emacs turns off:

@lisp
(with-eval-after-load 'eglot  ; in Doom: (after! eglot ...)
  (setq eglot-events-buffer-config '(:size 50000000 :format full)))
@end lisp

A snapshot contains your file and the others that the server opened; check it
before sharing it.

@node Credits
@chapter Credits

Lena builds on the ideas and code of many other projects in order to provide the experience it does now. In particular@comma{}
@itemize
@item
Lena is forked off @uref{https://codeberg.org/mekeor/nael, Nael}@comma{}
@item
dependency management and @samp{lena-rpc.el} are adapted from Doug Torrance's
@uref{https://github.com/d-torrance/lean4-mode, lean4-mode}@comma{} and @emph{Jan Mas Rovira}'s @uref{https://github.com/janmasrovira/neo-lean-mode, neo-lean-mode}@comma{}
@item
Lena's input method is generated from @uref{https://github.com/leanprover/vscode-lean4, vscode-lean4}@comma{}
@item
the infoview is modelled after @uref{https://github.com/Julian/lean.nvim, lean.nvim}@comma{} and @uref{https://github.com/leanprover/vscode-lean4, vscode-lean4}@comma{}
@item
the test fixtures are from @uref{https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean, iris-lean}
@end itemize

For a more detailed per-file breakdown@comma{} see the copyright header of each file.

